# {{TITLE}}

A contract-first Rust API generated by Minco {{MINCO_VERSION}}.

## Start

```bash
cp .env.example .env
set -a
source .env
set +a
cargo minco doctor
cargo minco config check
cargo minco contract sync --check
cargo minco check --with-cargo
cargo minco dev --dry-run --json
cargo minco dev
```

`cargo minco dev` starts only the local services declared by the application
graph, waits for readiness, applies the declared local migration, starts the API
and optional processes, and coordinates shutdown on Ctrl-C. The default
`MINCO_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=auto` uses Docker Compose when it is ready and falls
back to Apple Container 1.2.x on Apple silicon macOS 26 after `container system
start`.
Select a runtime explicitly when required:

```bash
MINCO_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=docker cargo minco dev
MINCO_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=apple cargo minco dev
```

The generated `infra/local/compose.yaml` remains application-owned and can be
customized for Docker, following the same publish-and-edit principle as Laravel
Sail. Apple Container runs Minco's declared PostgreSQL and Rustack services
through native OCI commands; application-specific Compose-only services still
require Docker or an explicit graph process. PostgreSQL data remains in a named
volume after shutdown. Minco verifies complete ownership metadata before reuse
or shutdown and never deletes persistent data. There is no implicit reset;
volume removal is a separate explicit data-loss operation.

The API listens at `http://127.0.0.1:3000` by default.

## Review migrations explicitly

Use the digest-bound lifecycle when a migration needs a separate review before
local execution, then start development with `cargo minco dev --no-migrate`:

```bash
{{DATABASE_SETUP}}
cargo minco db plan --set {{PACKAGE}}-{{DATABASE}} --json \
  > target/minco/migration-plan.json
MINCO_REVIEWED_MIGRATION_DIGEST="$(
  python3 -c 'import json; print(json.load(open("target/minco/migration-plan.json"))["digest"])'
)"
cargo minco db migrate \
  --set {{PACKAGE}}-{{DATABASE}} \
  --database-url-env DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL \
  --expected-plan-digest "$MINCO_REVIEWED_MIGRATION_DIGEST" \
  --receipt target/minco/migration-receipt.json
cargo minco dev --no-migrate
```

## Architecture

```text
HTTP delivery -> application -> domain
adapters ---------------------> application ports (as features are added)
composition -> delivery + application + adapters
```

The OpenAPI document in `openapi/openapi.yaml` is authoritative. Do not edit
`crates/api/src/generated.rs` manually. Migration lifecycle metadata lives in
`{{MIGRATION_DIR}}/.minco-migrations.toml`; do not edit an applied SQL file to
change metadata.

## JJ workflow

This repository is initialized as a colocated JJ/Git repository unless `cargo minco new` was run with `--vcs none`.

```bash
jj status
jj workspace add ../{{PACKAGE}}-M0-T01 --name M0-T01
```
